cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Eulerian walkers on Z^2 have range exponent 2/3"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/rotor-23"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the paper "Eulerian
  walkers on Z^2 have range exponent 2/3" (Bou-Rabee and Peres): recurrence,
  the limit shape and the range exponent 2/3 of the rotor walk with
  independent uniform initial rotors on the square lattice and on doubly
  periodic plane graphs of maximum degree three (Theorem 1.1), their
  extension to rotor laws close to uniform (Proposition 1.2), and a doubly
  periodic graph on which the walk is transient (Proposition 1.3).  One
  result the paper cites without proof, the Liggett-Schonmann-Stacey
  domination theorem, is an explicit hypothesis of the theorems that use it;
  the other six cited results are proved in the repository.  The development
  contains no sorry and no custom axiom, and each of the five main theorems
  has a Mathlib-only comparator challenge.
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - rotor walk
  - rotor-router
  - probability
license: Apache-2.0
references:
